    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0031" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg21"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/5–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-12T19:00:00+01:00">May 12, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:52 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1951. We asked Baeyens<anchor n="40" xml:id="d22-f1"/> whether Foreign Office
                    note transmitted Embtel 1941 meant that French intend raise with Secretary whole
                    question of defense SEA<anchor n="41" xml:id="d22-f2"/> against Chinese
                    Communists, French military situation in Indochina, our attitude toward Bao
                        Dai<anchor n="42" xml:id="d22-f3"/> regime, etc. After consulting
                        Parodi,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d22-f4"/> he has replied in negative saying
                    that present French plans are to confine discussions to eventual recognition
                    Chinese Communist regime in China with particular reference to special French
                    problems arising out of common frontier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d22-f1" n="40" xml:id="d22-f1-content">
                <p>Jacques Baeyens, Head of the Asia–Oceania Section of the French Foreign
                    Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d22-f2" n="41" xml:id="d22-f2-content">
                <p>Southeast Asia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d22-f3" n="42" xml:id="d22-f3-content">
                <p>Head of French Indochina, former Emperor of Annam.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d22-f4" n="43" xml:id="d22-f4-content">
                <p>Alexandre Parodi, Secretary General of the French Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
